SUMMARY:Modern Pop Art Experience with Michael Albert
DESCRIPTION:Join us as Michael Albert leads a Hands-On Collage workshop where participants will have the chance to create their own masterpieces using cereal boxes and other colorful cardboard packaging. All participants will receive a free signed poster of one of Albert’s creations as a special gift for joining him in this creative art making experience.  \nHis nationally renowned “Modern Pop Art Experience” Art programs will have toured more than 100 cities in six states this summer including: Alabama\, Mississippi\, Louisiana\, Georgia\, South Carolina & North Carolina.  Over the past 15 years he has been running this art enrichment program and brought it to more than 1\,500 libraries\, museums\, schools\, art and community centers in 48 states so far. \nAmerican Pop Artist Michael Albert was born and raised in New York on Long Island where he graduated from New York University with a business degree. Albert is the author of an artist autobiography titled\, “An Artist’s America” (Henry Holt\, 2008). His work has been described as a cross between Pop Art\, Cubism and Recycling.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/modern-pop-art-experience-with-michael-albert/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/download-7.png
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
